From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:30:00 +0200
Subject: ARM: dma-mapping: do not cross sparsemem sections in dcache clean loop

__dma_page_dev_to_cpu() walks the buffer with folio_next(). folio_next()
is pointer arithmetic on struct page. With SPARSEMEM and no VMEMMAP, the
mem_map of each section is a separate array. A buffer that crosses a
section makes the loop read a bogus struct page and oops in the MMC IRQ.

Seen on H3 with 512 MiB RAM: 0x40000000-0x5fffffff spans two 256 MiB
sections. Look up the next folio by pfn instead.

Fixes: cc24e9c0895c ("arm: implement the new page table range API")
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 arch/arm/mm/dma-mapping.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mm/dma-mapping.c b/arch/arm/mm/dma-mapping.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mm/dma-mapping.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mm/dma-mapping.c
@@ -718,7 +718,7 @@
 			size -= sz;
 			if (!size)
 				break;
-			folio = folio_next(folio);
+			folio = pfn_folio(folio_pfn(folio) + folio_nr_pages(folio));
 		}
 	}
 }
